section: compiler
issues: #28084
mrs: !16937
synopsis: ViewPatterns commoning improvements
description:

  When using :extension:`ViewPatterns`, GHC attempts to group occurrences of the
  same view expression in multiple branches of a function definition or case
  expression, e.g. ::

    f (expensive -> False) = ...
    f (expensive -> True) = ...

  This avoids applying the ``expensive`` expression more than once. This
  optimisation has been broken for most view expressions, including the above
  example, since GHC 8.0.1, and has been restored in this release.

  Note that :ghc-flag:`common subexpression elimination <-fcse>`, which is
  enabled under :ghc-flag:`-O`, could often recover this optimisation, limiting
  the impact of the bug on optimised programs.

  The limited notion of when two view pattern expressions are "the same" has
  also been extended to support type applications and expressions with a type
  signature. See the "Efficiency" section of :extension:`ViewPatterns` for more
  details.
